      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is deeply painful when advice feels dismissive, and it is completely understandable to feel that struggle is life itself, not just something to \"navigate.\" Right now, the focus might not need to be on a future \"point,\" but on finding a moment of profound rest from the pain you are in. If you feel unable to find help that truly *understands* the depth of your loss, please consider talking to a grief-specific therapist who can honor the gravity of what you are feeling.",
      "source": "target",
